            "timestamp": "2026-11-01T23:55:04.541808Z",
            "attributes": {
                "content": "[{\"text\": \"I would need to know why CBP recruitment is \\\"thin\\\" Is it a budgetary issue and why are the announcements with stated openings not being increased?\"}]"
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "gen_ai.assistant.message",
            "timestamp": "2026-11-01T23:55:04.541849Z",
            "attributes": {
                "content": "[{\"reasoningContent\": {\"reasoningText\": {\"text\": \"\", \"signature\": \"<stripped>"}}}, {\"text\": \"Not available\\nThe data cannot say why CBP Officer recruitment is thin or why announcements carry the openings they do. The records hold separation categories and posting openings, not reasons, and budget and appropriations are outside this review.\\n\\nThe figures already in this review show what \\\"thin\\\" means here. On August 1, 2026, eight CBP Officer announcements with stated openings were open, totaling eight openings, against 954 separations over the twelve months to August 2026, a coverage of 0.8%. Three more announcements say \\\"Many\\\" and are not counted, so the eight is a floor. Of the 954 separations, 586 were retirements.\\n\\nNearest answerable variants: the coverage ratio for CBP Officers at earlier dates, to show whether advertising has thinned over the year, or the separation categories by month, to show whether retirements are rising. I read \\\"thin\\\" as stated openings against separations; if you meant the number of announcements instead, say so.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\\"answer_value\\\": null, \\\"cited_tools\\\": []}\\n```\"}]"
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "gen_ai.user.message",
            "timestamp": "2026-11-01T23:55:04.541858Z",
            "attributes": {
                "content": "[{\"text\": \"Number of announcements would be helpful.\"}]"
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "gen_ai.choice",
            "timestamp": "2026-11-01T23:55:09.971177Z",
            "attributes": {
                "finish_reason": "end_turn",
                "message": "[{\"reasoningContent\": {\"reasoningText\": {\"text\": \"\", \"signature\": \"<stripped>"}}}, {\"text\": \"Verified\\nOn August 1, 2026, 11 CBP Officer announcements were open (the 1895 series, including supervisory and program-manager titles). Eight state a number of openings, totaling eight, and three say \\\"Many.\\\" Five give no state and two list Virginia. Because the count is an upper bound, announcements filled or cancelled before their closing dates are not visible. I read this as announcements open on August 1, 2026; if you meant the number opened over the trailing twelve months, say so.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\\"answer_value\\\": 11, \\\"cited_tools\\\": [\\\"workforce__semantic__open_postings\\\"]}\\n```\"}]"
            }
        }
    ],
