            "attributes": {
                "content": "[{\"reasoningContent\": {\"reasoningText\": {\"text\": \"\", \"signature\": \"<stripped>"}}}, {\"text\": \"Exploratory\\nCBP's workforce as of the August 2026 snapshot was 70,843, and 28.9% had 20 or more years of federal service (62.0% had 10 or more). That puts CBP second only to ICE on the 20-year share and second only to CISA on the 10-year share. Years of service is a proxy for retirement exposure, not retirement eligibility, which depends on age and retirement coverage, and the data has no forward projection.\\n\\n**CBP occupations, August 2026 (top 10 by headcount; the other 105 series are summed below the table)**\\n\\n| Series | Occupation | Headcount | With 20+ years | 20+ share |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1895 | CBP Officers | 27,650 | 8,732 | 31.6% |\\n| 1896 | Border Patrol agents | 22,464 | 5,513 | 24.5% |\\n| 0401 | Natural resources and biological sciences | 2,833 | 852 | 30.1% |\\n| 1801 | Inspection, investigation, enforcement and compliance | 2,247 | 910 | 40.5% |\\n| 0301 | Miscellaneous administration and program | 2,017 | 642 | 31.8% |\\n| 1802 | Compliance inspection and support (screeners) | 1,958 | 223 | 11.4% |\\n| 0343 | Management and program analysis | 1,446 | 478 | 33.1% |\\n| 2210 | IT management | 1,235 | 228 | 18.5% |\\n| 1889 | Import compliance | 1,120 | 405 | 36.2% |\\n| 0340 | Program management | 951 | 429 | 45.1% |\\n| All other 105 series | | 6,922 | 2,064 | 29.8% |\\n\\nI added the rows: the top 10 sum to 63,921 staff, and the remaining 105 series add 6,922, giving the 70,843 total.\\n\\n**CBP against the other components (all occupations, August 2026)**\\n\\n| Component | Headcount | 20+ years | 10+ years |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| CBP | 70,843 | 28.9% | 62.0% |\\n| ICE | 28,674 | 29.6% | 57.5% |\\n| TSA | 59,342 | 21.2% | 46.4% |\\n| USCIS | 20,327 | 21.1% | 59.8% |\\n| CISA | 2,204 | 22.9% | 65.8% |\\n| FEMA | 20,208 | 10.4% | 33.9% |\\n\\nI read \\\"CPB\\\" as CBP, all occupations, as of August 2026, and the comparison as years of service across the six components; if you meant CBP Officers only, that is the 1895 row, and if you want age-based eligibility, it is not in the data.\\n\\n```sql\\nWITH series_counts AS (\\n  SELECT\\n    workforce_snapshot.occupational_series_code,\\n    workforce_snapshot.occupational_series,\\n    COUNT(*) AS headcount,\\n    SUM(CASE WHEN workforce_snapshot.length_of_service_years >= 20 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS headcount_20_plus_years\\n  FROM workforce.semantic.workforce_snapshot\\n  WHERE workforce_snapshot.snapshot_month = DATE '2026-08-01'\\n    AND workforce_snapshot.agency_subelement_code = 'HSBD'\\n    AND workforce_snapshot.occupational_series_code IS NOT NULL\\n    AND workforce_snapshot.occupational_series IS NOT NULL\\n  GROUP BY\\n    workforce_snapshot.occupational_series_code,\\n    workforce_snapshot.occupational_series\\n)\\nSELECT\\n  series_counts.occupational_series_code,\\n  series_counts.occupational_series,\\n  series_counts.headcount,\\n  series_counts.headcount_20_plus_years,\\n  SUM(series_counts.headcount) OVER () AS total_headcount_all_series\\nFROM series_counts\\nORDER BY series_counts.headcount DESC, series_counts.occupational_series_code, series_counts.occupational_series\\n```\\n\\n```json\\n{\\\"answer_value\\\": [{\\\"key\\\": \\\"1895\\\", \\\"value\\\": 27650}, {\\\"key\\\": \\\"1896\\\", \\\"value\\\": 22464}, {\\\"key\\\": \\\"0401\\\", \\\"value\\\": 2833}, {\\\"key\\\": \\\"1801\\\", \\\"value\\\": 2247}, {\\\"key\\\": \\\"0301\\\", \\\"value\\\": 2017}, {\\\"key\\\": \\\"1802\\\", \\\"value\\\": 1958}, {\\\"key\\\": \\\"0343\\\", \\\"value\\\": 1446}, {\\\"key\\\": \\\"2210\\\", \\\"value\\\": 1235}, {\\\"key\\\": \\\"1889\\\", \\\"value\\\": 1120}, {\\\"key\\\": \\\"0340\\\", \\\"value\\\": 951}], \\\"cited_tools\\\": [\\\"workforce__semantic__length_of_service_profile\\\", \\\"genie\\\"]}\\n```\"}]"
