                "content": "[{\"reasoningContent\": {\"reasoningText\": {\"text\": \"\", \"signature\": \"<stripped>"}}}, {\"text\": \"Verified\\n\\nDraft for OPM:\\nCBP Officers recorded 475 accessions against 594 planned hires in FY2026 Q1 (October to December 2025), a variance of -119 (-20.0%). Two findings bear on the gap: over the twelve months to August 2026 the cell separated 954 people, a rate of 0.0351 that is the same with and without the 2025 deferred resignation wave, and 586 of those separations (61%) were retirements; and only eight announcements with stated openings were open on August 1, 2026, totaling eight openings (three more say \\\"Many\\\"), against those 954 separations, a coverage of 0.8%. The quarter is not closed, so late OPM files will add accessions and the variance will narrow, and separation counts will also grow as late reports arrive. We request that CBP open enough CBP Officer announcements with stated openings to cover the 586 retirements in the trailing twelve months, and that the agency report the updated FY2026 Q1 accession count once later files are in.\\n\\nI read this as the open cell, CBP Officers in FY2026 Q1, with attrition over the twelve months to August 2026; if you meant another cell or a different attrition window, say so.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\\"answer_value\\\": -119, \\\"cited_tools\\\": [\\\"workforce__semantic__plan_variance\\\", \\\"workforce__semantic__separation_rate\\\", \\\"workforce__semantic__open_postings\\\"]}\\n```\"}]"
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "gen_ai.user.message",
            "timestamp": "2026-11-01T23:55:04.539979Z",
            "attributes": {
                "content": "[{\"text\": \"I would need to know why CBP recruitment is \\\"thin\\\" Is it a budgetary issue and why are the announcements with stated openings not being increased?\"}]"
            }
