        {
            "name": "gen_ai.choice",
            "timestamp": "2026-11-02T00:17:32.495724Z",
            "attributes": {
                "finish_reason": "end_turn",
                "message": "[{\"reasoningContent\": {\"reasoningText\": {\"text\": \"\", \"signature\": \"<stripped>"}}}, {\"text\": \"Exploratory\\nFrom September 2025 to October 2026, 463 CBP postings listed the CBP Officer series: 337 (73%) at grades 13 to 14, 94 (20%) at grades 5 to 12, and 32 (7%) at grade 15 and above. The 13 to 14 band was the largest in every month, from 58% in March 2026 to 86% in December 2025. Stated openings were 708 in total, but postings that say \\\"Many\\\" count as zero, so openings are understated.\\n\\n| Period (months) | Postings | Grades 5 to 12 | Grades 13 to 14 | Grade 15 and above | Stated openings |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| September 2025 | 37 | 11 | 25 | 1 | 107 |\\n| October to December 2025 (FY2026 Q1) | 86 | 14 | 71 | 1 | 132 |\\n| January to March 2026 (FY2026 Q2) | 78 | 18 | 53 | 7 | 113 |\\n| April to June 2026 (FY2026 Q3) | 104 | 21 | 71 | 12 | 156 |\\n| July to August 2026 | 79 | 18 | 54 | 7 | 101 |\\n| September 2026 | 45 | 4 | 38 | 3 | 62 |\\n| October 2026 | 34 | 8 | 25 | 1 | 37 |\\n\\nThe data shows what was advertised and at which grades. It does not show why, and it cannot answer the Director's other questions. There are no applicant records, no performance ratings, no training or competency records, and no separation reasons beyond the four categories. Comparison with agencies outside DHS is outside this review. The closest in-scope comparison is the other DHS components, which I can set against CBP on years of service. To close the gaps, the analyst could ask OPM and the agency for applicant flow by posting (applicants, referred, selected), grade on staff records so staff and posting grade mix can be compared, performance rating distributions and training completion by series and grade, and reasons recorded at separation.\\n\\nI read \\\"grade mix over time\\\" as the grade band of CBP postings for the CBP Officer series, by month of opening; if you meant the grade mix of staff, the review's calculations do not report staff by grade.\\n\\n```sql\\nWITH `filtered` AS (\\n  SELECT\\n    DATE_TRUNC('MONTH', `open_date`) AS `open_month`,\\n    CASE\\n      WHEN CAST(`minimum_grade` AS INT) BETWEEN 5 AND 9 THEN '5 to 9'\\n      WHEN CAST(`minimum_grade` AS INT) BETWEEN 10 AND 12 THEN '10 to 12'\\n      WHEN CAST(`minimum_grade` AS INT) BETWEEN 13 AND 14 THEN '13 to 14'\\n      WHEN CAST(`minimum_grade` AS INT) >= 15 THEN '15 and above'\\n      ELSE NULL\\n    END AS `minimum_grade_band`,\\n    COALESCE(`total_openings`, 0) AS `stated_openings`\\n  FROM `workforce`.`semantic`.`job_posting`\\n  WHERE `agency_subelement_code` = 'HSBD'\\n    AND `open_date` >= DATE '2025-09-01'\\n    AND `open_date` < DATE '2026-11-01'\\n    AND `open_date` IS NOT NULL\\n    AND `minimum_grade` IS NOT NULL\\n    AND array_contains(`occupational_series_codes`, '1895')\\n), `grouped` AS (\\n  SELECT\\n    `open_month`,\\n    `minimum_grade_band`,\\n    COUNT(*) AS `postings`,\\n    SUM(`stated_openings`) AS `total_openings`\\n  FROM `filtered`\\n  WHERE `minimum_grade_band` IS NOT NULL\\n  GROUP BY `open_month`, `minimum_grade_band`\\n)\\nSELECT\\n  `open_month`,\\n  `minimum_grade_band`,\\n  `postings`,\\n  `total_openings`,\\n  SUM(`postings`) OVER (PARTITION BY `open_month`) AS `month_total_postings`\\nFROM `grouped`\\nORDER BY\\n  `open_month`,\\n  CASE `minimum_grade_band`\\n    WHEN '5 to 9' THEN 1\\n    WHEN '10 to 12' THEN 2\\n    WHEN '13 to 14' THEN 3\\n    WHEN '15 and above' THEN 4\\n    ELSE 5\\n  END\\n```\\n\\n```json\\n{\\\"answer_value\\\": [{\\\"key\\\": \\\"13 to 14\\\", \\\"value\\\": 337}, {\\\"key\\\": \\\"5 to 12\\\", \\\"value\\\": 94}, {\\\"key\\\": \\\"15 and above\\\", \\\"value\\\": 32}], \\\"cited_tools\\\": [\\\"genie\\\"]}\\n```\"}]"
            }
        }
