        {
            "name": "gen_ai.assistant.message",
            "timestamp": "2026-11-02T00:17:07.939873Z",
            "attributes": {
                "content": "[{\"reasoningContent\": {\"reasoningText\": {\"text\": \"\", \"signature\": \"<stripped>"}}}, {\"text\": \"Not available\\n\\\"Many\\\" is the posting's own wording for an unstated number of openings, and the data holds only that word, so it cannot tell you whether a posting means two openings or two hundred. The three CBP Officer announcements that say \\\"Many\\\" carry control numbers 878058100 (grades 5 to 7), 878058600 (grade 9) and 875468500 (grade 13), and the openings figure is on each posting on USAJOBS. Until those are read, the eight stated openings are the only countable figure, and the 0.8% coverage is a floor.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\\"answer_value\\\": null, \\\"cited_tools\\\": []}\\n```\"}]"
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "gen_ai.user.message",
            "timestamp": "2026-11-02T00:17:07.939879Z",
            "attributes": {
                "content": "[{\"text\": \"When OPM collects their data by grade is it possible to find out which positions are applicants not applying to? Trying to find out if the higher graded positions are the hardest to fill.  Would like to know if the lower graded positions are tough to get applicants.\"}]"
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "gen_ai.assistant.message",
            "timestamp": "2026-11-02T00:17:07.939909Z",
            "attributes": {
                "content": "[{\"reasoningContent\": {\"reasoningText\": {\"text\": \"\", \"signature\": \"<stripped>"}}}, {\"text\": \"Not available\\nThe review's data has no applicant records, so it cannot show which positions applicants skip, and it has no grade field for staff to test whether higher grades are harder to fill. Posting counts do not measure difficulty either: an announcement can be open for weeks and still draw applicants.\\n\\nThe nearest answerable view is the grades on the 11 CBP Officer announcements open on August 1, 2026. Eight state openings and sit at grades 12 to 14 (three at 14, three at 13, two at 12). The three \\\"Many\\\" announcements sit at grades 5 to 7, 9 and 13, so the only lower-grade announcements open that day have no stated openings. I read \\\"hard to fill\\\" as openings advertised without applicant data; if you want the advertised grade mix over time, say so.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\\"answer_value\\\": null, \\\"cited_tools\\\": []}\\n```\"}]"
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "gen_ai.user.message",
            "timestamp": "2026-11-02T00:17:07.939927Z",
            "attributes": {
                "content": "[{\"text\": \"Grade mix over time would be helpful.  It is hard to prepare for a briefing for the Director without having the \\\"why\\\" behind the numbers which is what is also needed in addition to the numbers (the what).  The why is what Director will be interested in knowing after seeing the numbers and what these numbers tell me is helpful because they show that there are issues to be addressed and Director will definitely ask about recruitment numbers, hiring pluses and minuses, HR development (does it meet workforce development goals and actual training needs), performance assessments, etc. All of these areas need to be analyzed using a model that can help Director get a true picture of what is happening in the organization.  Director will ask these kinds of questions. Director will want a comparison with other larger organizations of like size to make some comparisons. Just seeing the numbers and percentages is helpful but if OPM could provide more details it would help Director of CBP and other elements to address issues like recruitment and skills mix. What can be done about not having enough OPM data to systemtically address issue?\"}]"
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "gen_ai.assistant.message",
            "timestamp": "2026-11-02T00:17:07.939951Z",
            "attributes": {
                "content": "[{\"reasoningContent\": {\"reasoningText\": {\"text\": \"\", \"signature\": \"<stripped>"}}}, {\"toolUse\": {\"toolUseId\": \"toolu_01RJpEZKskvdriUzEVKXhczt\", \"name\": \"one_off_query\", \"input\": {\"question\": \"For CBP (agency subelement code HSBD) job postings that list occupational series 1895, count the postings by calendar month of open date from September 2025 through October 2026. Within each month, break the postings down by minimum grade band (grades 5 to 9, 10 to 12, 13 to 14, and 15 and above), and give the number of postings and the sum of stated total openings in each month and grade band (postings with no stated opening count as zero openings). Return one row per month and grade band, with the total postings for each month as well.\"}}}]"
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "gen_ai.tool.message",
            "timestamp": "2026-11-02T00:17:07.939982Z",
            "attributes": {
                "content": "[{\"toolResult\": {\"status\": \"success\", \"content\": [{\"text\": \"{\\\"sql\\\": \\\"WITH `filtered` AS (\\\\n  SELECT\\\\n    DATE_TRUNC('MONTH', `open_date`) AS `open_month`,\\\\n    CASE\\\\n      WHEN CAST(`minimum_grade` AS INT) BETWEEN 5 AND 9 THEN '5 to 9'\\\\n      WHEN CAST(`minimum_grade` AS INT) BETWEEN 10 AND 12 THEN '10 to 12'\\\\n      WHEN CAST(`minimum_grade` AS INT) BETWEEN 13 AND 14 THEN '13 to 14'\\\\n      WHEN CAST(`minimum_grade` AS INT) >= 15 THEN '15 and above'\\\\n      ELSE NULL\\\\n    END AS `minimum_grade_band`,\\\\n    COALESCE(`total_openings`, 0) AS `stated_openings`\\\\n  FROM `workforce`.`semantic`.`job_posting`\\\\n  WHERE `agency_subelement_code` = 'HSBD'\\\\n    AND `open_date` >= DATE '2025-09-01'\\\\n    AND `open_date` < DATE '2026-11-01'\\\\n    AND `open_date` IS NOT NULL\\\\n    AND `minimum_grade` IS NOT NULL\\\\n    AND array_contains(`occupational_series_codes`, '1895')\\\\n), `grouped` AS (\\\\n  SELECT\\\\n    `open_month`,\\\\n    `minimum_grade_band`,\\\\n    COUNT(*) AS `postings`,\\\\n    SUM(`stated_openings`) AS `total_openings`\\\\n  FROM `filtered`\\\\n  WHERE `minimum_grade_band` IS NOT NULL\\\\n  GROUP BY `open_month`, `minimum_grade_band`\\\\n)\\\\nSELECT\\\\n  `open_month`,\\\\n  `minimum_grade_band`,\\\\n  `postings`,\\\\n  `total_openings`,\\\\n  SUM(`postings`) OVER (PARTITION BY `open_month`) AS `month_total_postings`\\\\nFROM `grouped`\\\\nORDER BY\\\\n  `open_month`,\\\\n  CASE `minimum_grade_band`\\\\n    WHEN '5 to 9' THEN 1\\\\n    WHEN '10 to 12' THEN 2\\\\n    WHEN '13 to 14' THEN 3\\\\n    WHEN '15 and above' THEN 4\\\\n    ELSE 5\\\\n  END\\\", \\\"statement_id\\\": \\\"01f1d652-ae60-1f83-9223-f577906aa742\\\", \\\"message_id\\\": \\\"01f1d652a56614faa6032847f0f7c474\\\", \\\"columns\\\": [\\\"open_month\\\", \\\"minimum_grade_band\\\", \\\"postings\\\", \\\"total_openings\\\", \\\"month_total_postings\\\"], \\\"rows\\\": [[\\\"2025-09-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"5 to 9\\\", 4, 0, 37], [\\\"2025-09-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"10 to 12\\\", 7, 7, 37], [\\\"2025-09-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"13 to 14\\\", 25, 99, 37], [\\\"2025-09-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"15 and above\\\", 1, 1, 37], [\\\"2025-10-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"5 to 9\\\", 1, 3, 26], [\\\"2025-10-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"10 to 12\\\", 5, 3, 26], [\\\"2025-10-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"13 to 14\\\", 20, 35, 26], [\\\"2025-11-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"5 to 9\\\", 2, 0, 31], [\\\"2025-11-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"10 to 12\\\", 3, 2, 31], [\\\"2025-11-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"13 to 14\\\", 26, 49, 31], [\\\"2025-12-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"5 to 9\\\", 2, 0, 29], [\\\"2025-12-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"10 to 12\\\", 1, 1, 29], [\\\"2025-12-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"13 to 14\\\", 25, 38, 29], [\\\"2025-12-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"15 and above\\\", 1, 1, 29], [\\\"2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"5 to 9\\\", 2, 0, 18], [\\\"2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"10 to 12\\\", 1, 1, 18], [\\\"2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"13 to 14\\\", 14, 14, 18], [\\\"2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"15 and above\\\", 1, 1, 18], [\\\"2026-02-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"5 to 9\\\", 2, 0, 24], [\\\"2026-02-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"10 to 12\\\", 4, 10, 24], [\\\"2026-02-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"13 to 14\\\", 18, 47, 24], [\\\"2026-03-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"5 to 9\\\", 3, 1, 36], [\\\"2026-03-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"10 to 12\\\", 6, 9, 36], [\\\"2026-03-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"13 to 14\\\", 21, 26, 36], [\\\"2026-03-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"15 and above\\\", 6, 4, 36], [\\\"2026-04-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"5 to 9\\\", 4, 25, 49], [\\\"2026-04-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"10 to 12\\\", 4, 4, 49], [\\\"2026-04-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"13 to 14\\\", 32, 30, 49], [\\\"2026-04-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"15 and above\\\", 9, 9, 49], [\\\"2026-05-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"5 to 9\\\", 3, 10, 36], [\\\"2026-05-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"10 to 12\\\", 6, 6, 36], [\\\"2026-05-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"13 to 14\\\", 25, 38, 36], [\\\"2026-05-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"15 and above\\\", 2, 2, 36], [\\\"2026-06-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"5 to 9\\\", 3, 10, 19], [\\\"2026-06-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"10 to 12\\\", 1, 4, 19], [\\\"2026-06-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"13 to 14\\\", 14, 17, 19], [\\\"2026-06-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"15 and above\\\", 1, 1, 19], [\\\"2026-07-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"5 to 9\\\", 3, 0, 40], [\\\"2026-07-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"10 to 12\\\", 5, 4, 40], [\\\"2026-07-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"13 to 14\\\", 28, 52, 40], [\\\"2026-07-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"15 and above\\\", 4, 4, 40], [\\\"2026-08-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"5 to 9\\\", 3, 0, 39], [\\\"2026-08-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"10 to 12\\\", 7, 11, 39], [\\\"2026-08-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"13 to 14\\\", 26, 28, 39], [\\\"2026-08-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"15 and above\\\", 3, 2, 39], [\\\"2026-09-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"5 to 9\\\", 3, 2, 45], [\\\"2026-09-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"10 to 12\\\", 1, 1, 45], [\\\"2026-09-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"13 to 14\\\", 38, 56, 45], [\\\"2026-09-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"15 and above\\\", 3, 3, 45], [\\\"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"5 to 9\\\", 1, 0, 34], [\\\"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"10 to 12\\\", 7, 6, 34], [\\\"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"13 to 14\\\", 25, 30, 34], [\\\"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z\\\", \\\"15 and above\\\", 1, 1, 34]], \\\"row_count\\\": 53, \\\"truncated\\\": false, \\\"text\\\": [\\\"Examples include:\\\\n- **2025-09:** **37** total postings \\\\u2014 **5 to 9:** 4 postings / 0 openings; **10 to 12:** 7 / 7; **13 to 14:** 25 / 99; **15 and above:** 1 / 1.\\\\n- **2025-10:** **26** total postings \\\\u2014 **5 to 9:** 1 / 3; **10 to 12:** 5 / 3; **13 to 14:** 20 / 35.\\\\n- **2025-11:** **31** total postings \\\\u2014 **5 to 9:** 2 / 0; **10 to 12:** 3 / 2; **13 to 14:** 26 / 49.\\\\n- **2025-12:** **29** total postings \\\\u2014 **5 to 9:** 2 / 0; **10 to 12:** 1 / 1; **13 to 14:** 25 / 38; **15 and above:** 1 / 1.\\\\n- **2026-01:** **18** total postings \\\\u2014 **5 to 9:** 2 / 0; **10 to 12:** 1 / 1; **13 to 14:** 14 / 14; **15 and above:** 1 / 1.\\\\nAcross all 53 month-and-grade-band rows shown, the **13 to 14** band is the largest in every month, while monthly total postings range from **18** in **2026-01** to **49** in **2026-04**.\\\"]}\"}], \"toolUseId\": \"toolu_01RJpEZKskvdriUzEVKXhczt\"}}]"
            }
